{"symbol":"MRK.DE","area":"europe","updated":"2026-11-13T22:51:02Z","info":{"address1":"Frankfurter Strasse 250","city":"Darmstadt","zip":"64293","country":"Germany","phone":"49 6151 72 0","fax":"49 6151 72 2000","website":"https://www.merckgroup.com","industry":"Drug Manufacturers - Specialty & Generic","industryKey":"drug-manufacturers-specialty-generic","industryDisp":"Drug Manufacturers - Specialty & Generic","sector":"Healthcare","sectorKey":"healthcare","sectorDisp":"Healthcare","longBusinessSummary":"Merck KGaA operates as a science and technology company in Europe, North America, Latin America, Middle East and Africa, and the Asia Pacific. The Life Science segment offers products, solutions, and services to academic, research and diagnostic labs, biotech, and pharmaceutical companies, as well as the industrial sector; reagents, consumables, devices, instruments, software, and services for research, production, and testing to lab water instruments, microbiology and biomonitoring products, test assays, analytical reagents, and flow cytometry kits and instruments. This segment also provides traditional and novel therapies, such as ration devices, chromatography resins, single-use systems, process chemicals, and excipients for bioprocessing; contract development, manufacturing and testing services, which supports customers from preclinical phases to commercialization. The Healthcare segment discovers, develops, manufactures, and markets prescription drugs and biopharmaceuticals to the therapeutic areas of oncology, rare diseases, neurology and immunology, fertility, cardiovascular, and metabolic and endocrinological disorders. The Electronics segment offers advanced dielectric and metallic materials; photoresist, anti-reflective coating, and material lithography products; clean and selective etch chemistries; materials for chemical-mechanical planarization; high-purity gases for semiconductor manufacturing; and develops and installs delivery equipment for handling of specialty chemicals and gases for semiconductor manufacturing; develops modulating, creating, engineering, and guiding light; and material solutions in liquid crystals, OLED materials, and photoresists. It has in-licensing agreement with Abbisko Therapeutics Co. Ltd., China on drug candidates for the treatment of tenosynovial giant cell tumor; and strategic partnership with Versant Ventures to advance treatments for rare genetic cardiomyopathies. The company was founded in 1668 and is headquartered in Darmstadt, Germany. Merck KGaA operates as a subsidiary of E. Merck KG.","fullTimeEmployees":61949,"companyOfficers":[{"maxAge":1,"name":"Dr. Kai  Beckmann","age":60,"title":"CEO & Chair of Management Board","yearBorn":1965,"fiscalYear":2025,"totalPay":4933000,"exercisedValue":0,"unexercisedValue":0},{"maxAge":1,"name":"Ms. Helene  von Roeder","age":55,"title":"CFO & Member of Executive Board","yearBorn":1970,"fiscalYear":2025,"totalPay":4765000,"exercisedValue":0,"unexercisedValue":0},{"maxAge":1,"name":"Mr. Danny Pinhas Bar-Zohar M.D.","age":55,"title":"Member of the Executive Board & CEO of Healthcare","yearBorn":1970,"fiscalYear":2025,"totalPay":1224800,"exercisedValue":0,"unexercisedValue":0},{"maxAge":1,"name":"Mr. Jean Charles Wirth","age":52,"title":"Member of the Executive Board & CEO Life Science","yearBorn":1973,"fiscalYear":2025,"totalPay":1207800,"exercisedValue":0,"unexercisedValue":0},{"maxAge":1,"name":"Ms. Khadija Ben Hammada","age":45,"title":"Member of the Executive Board & Chief People Officer","yearBorn":1980,"fiscalYear":2025,"totalPay":1210000,"exercisedValue":0,"unexercisedValue":0},{"maxAge":1,"name":"Mr. Benjamin  Hein","title":"Member of Management Board & CEO of Electronics Business Sector","fiscalYear":2025,"exercisedValue":0,"unexercisedValue":0},{"maxAge":1,"name":"Florian  Schraeder","title":"Head of Investor Relations","fiscalYear":2025,"exercisedValue":0,"unexercisedValue":0},{"maxAge":1,"name":"Mr. Axel  Lober","title":"Head of 